    public UpdateMarkerData(@NotNull World world) {
        super(1, true);
        this.world = world;
        this.executor = Pl3xMap.api().getRenderExecutor();
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        if (this.running) {
            return;
        }

        this.running = true;
        this.future = CompletableFuture.runAsync(this::update, this.executor)
                .thenRun(() -> this.running = false);
    }

    private void update() {
        for (Layer layer : world.getLayerRegistry().getValues()) {
            if (!layer.shouldShowControls()) {
                continue;
            }

            long now = System.currentTimeMillis();
            long last = lastUpdated.getOrDefault(layer.getKey(), 0L);
            if (now - last < layer.getUpdateInterval() * 1000L) {
                continue;
            }

            lastUpdated.put(layer.getKey(), now);

            JsonObject json = new JsonObject();
            json.addProperty("key", layer.getKey());
            json.add("markers", gson.toJsonTree(layer.getMarkers()));

            Path path = world.getMarkersDirectory().resolve(layer.getKey() + ".json");
            try {
                FileUtil.writeJson(gson.toJson(json), path);
            } catch (Exception e) {
                Logger.severe("Failed to write marker data for layer " + layer.getKey(), e);
            }
        }
    }

    private static class Adapter implements JsonSerializer<Marker<?>> {
        @Override
        public JsonElement serialize(Marker<?> src, Type typeOfSrc, JsonSerializationContext context) {
            JsonObject json = new JsonObject();
            json.addProperty("type", src.getType());
            json.addProperty("key", src.getKey());

            JsonObject data = new JsonObject();
            if (src instanceof Circle c) {
                data.addProperty("x", c.getCenterX());
                data.addProperty("z", c.getCenterZ());
                data.addProperty("r", c.getRadius());
            } else if (src instanceof Rectangle r) {
                data.addProperty("x1", r.getX1());
                data.addProperty("z1", r.getZ1());
                data.addProperty("x2", r.getX2());
                data.addProperty("z2", r.getZ2());
            } else if (src instanceof Icon i) {
                data.addProperty("x", i.getX());
                data.addProperty("z", i.getZ());
                data.addProperty("img", i.getImage());
                data.addProperty("w", i.getWidth());
                data.addProperty("h", i.getHeight());
            }
            // Other marker types would be handled here similarly...

            json.add("data", data);
            if (src.getOptions() != null) {
                json.add("options", context.serialize(src.getOptions()));
            }
            return json;
        }
    }
```

Explanation:
The `UpdateMarkerData` class is a scheduled `Task` responsible for periodically serializing marker data from a `World`'s layers into JSON files. 

1. **Constructor**: Initializes the task to run every second (`super(1, true)`) and assigns the world and the global render executor.
2. **run()**: Implements a non-blocking execution pattern using a `CompletableFuture` and a `running` flag to ensure that if a previous update cycle is still processing, a new one doesn't start.
3. **update()**: Iterates through all registered layers in the world. It checks if the layer is visible and if the `updateInterval` (defined in the `Layer` class) has elapsed. If so, it collects the markers and writes them to a JSON file in the world's markers directory using `FileUtil.writeJson`.
4. **Adapter**: A custom Gson `JsonSerializer` that converts `Marker` objects into the specific JSON format expected by the frontend (splitting the marker into `type`, `key`, `data`, and `options`).

